{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/926659-small-town-requiem","id":926659,"title":"Small town Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-05T14:56:44-07:00","id":926659,"title":"Small town Requiem","content":"Hey guys, <br /> I was thinking about starting a game based on a small town. 60,000. I'm only going to have 3 people in the coterie, and I don't think I'll have many other vampires in the city. Maybe only the coterie's sires and such. Right now I am trying to brainstorm ideas for the game. I want to keep it smaller with not as much focus on large scale Kindred politics (which is what I normally run). I want to play with lower management themes such as &quot;What does the group do when a biker gang of Brujah roles through town and causes masquerade breaches and other issues?&quot; <br /> <br /> Any other ideas you think I could play off of? What do small town vampires do? What would you do if you were running this chronicle? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T15:59:45-07:00","id":926696,"title":"","content":"Danse Macabre has a whole section on Tier 1 games, wheere are few Kindred, none of them are very old, and the Covenants largely don't exist. It's also some of the best stuff I've ever read in all of thr CofD library; I'd start there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:15:02-07:00","id":926700,"title":"","content":"Given the situation you described, I think the way I would go about is thus: First, figure out why their sires embraced them. What was the agenda? The vampires of a town just doubled the predator population -- to what end? <br /> <br /> Next, deal with the situation of new vampires in a world of mortals. Chances are, there are dozens of people who know the PCs on sight -- why doesn't my buddy come to class/work/picnics/baseball games anymore? The coterie members now have to deal with hiding their natures as well as coming to terms with their friends now also being potential meals. Or blood slaves.<br /> <br /> Once they start to get a handle on that, then have them explore the perks of being vampires in a setting where they don't have much competition. Let them pursue their dreams. This one would love to take over the company that fired him. There are ways to do that, and lets see what consequences come from it. That one wants to clean up the streets she grew up on. How? By preying on pushers and muggers? By taking over a gang and getting rid of the other gangs? By spying on the local criminals and feeding info to a detective?<br /> <br /> Once they have the lay of the land -- once they are somewhat secure, once they have a stake (so to speak) in how things go, once they have something to lose... THEN bring in the biker vamps, or some colonizing Invictus, or a elder on the lam. <br /> <br /> You've got 60,000 people to play with; hell, you have a town, which should have it's own personality. Make it mean more to the players than just a drab backdrop on which to enact Kindred politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:38:33-07:00","id":926759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/926659-small-town-requiem?p=926696#post926696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Danse Macabre has a whole section on Tier 1 games, there are few Kindred, none of them are very old, and the Covenants largely don't exist. It's also some of the best stuff I've ever read in all of the CofD library; I'd start there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah-ha that was exactly what I was looking for... I remembered there being some information on tiered playing (like in Hunter: The Vigil) for vampire, but I kept looking in Damnation City and just couldn't find it. Thank you very much.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got 60,000 people to play with; hell, you have a town, which should have it's own personality. Make it mean more to the players than just a drab backdrop on which to enact Kindred politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some great ideas. I have always sort of struggled with conceptualizing some overarching ideas. <br /> <br /> <br /> One of my players wants to be a member of the Circle of the Crone, which is great, I always encourage players to branch out and try to immerse their characters into the setting. Our idea is that as a newer vampire they traveled to a larger capital city and was introduced to organized Kindred for the first time (in this case the Crones). She obtained her first dot in covenant status from meeting down there which then let her learn Cruac. <br /> We've talked and she thinks it would be cool if she brought Cruac back to this little town, and tried to get the other coterie member's to give it a shot. The part that I'm not sure about is the status dot in Circle of the Crone. I want to make sure that it comes up, and isn't just an additional cost to learning Cruac, all the while keeping it low scale. We talked about the potential of later taking dots in Mystery Cult Initiation, to have Ghouls and later mortals join a paganistic religion. Would her status in the Circle of the Crone only come up if they visited or is there a good way I could incorporate that? <br /> In the past I've allowed players to add their status dots into social rolls, but I fear that won't come up much this only a handful of Kindred in the town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T19:15:54-07:00","id":926780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/926659-small-town-requiem?p=926759#post926759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players wants to be a member of the Circle of the Crone, which is great, I always encourage players to branch out and try to immerse their characters into the setting. Our idea is that as a newer vampire they traveled to a larger capital city and was introduced to organized Kindred for the first time (in this case the Crones). She obtained her first dot in covenant status from meeting down there which then let her learn Cruac.<br /> We've talked and she thinks it would be cool if she brought Cruac back to this little town, and tried to get the other coterie member's to give it a shot. The part that I'm not sure about is the status dot in Circle of the Crone. I want to make sure that it comes up, and isn't just an additional cost to learning Cruac, all the while keeping it low scale. We talked about the potential of later taking dots in Mystery Cult Initiation, to have Ghouls and later mortals join a paganistic religion. Would her status in the Circle of the Crone only come up if they visited or is there a good way I could incorporate that?<br /> In the past I've allowed players to add their status dots into social rolls, but I fear that won't come up much this only a handful of Kindred in the town.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle of the Crone is great for this in that they don't really <i>have</i> anything like a monolithic culture. They are pretty much an umbrella of a bunch of different usually-pagan blood cults. So you don't really have to worry about your character deviating from &quot;doctrine&quot; - there isn't any! Or rather, she'll write her own version in that town. Maybe it will die out, maybe it will spread from there (Plot Seed: some neonate disciple seeks to convert to your flavor of the Circle and spread the message far and wide).<br /> <br /> As for Status, there's two ways to look at it - one, there aren't many members, so not much intra-Covenant use, but two, being the only real local members, you are pretty much certain to have top Status.<br /> <hr /><br /> Are you planning on any cross-over? Because you might be able to work in some political plots by negotiating with other supernaturals. It's easier to &quot;speak for the vampires&quot; when you represent a good percentage of said vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T21:57:23-07:00","id":926845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/926659-small-town-requiem?p=926759#post926759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of my players wants to be a member of the Circle of the Crone, which is great, I always encourage players to branch out and try to immerse their characters into the setting. Our idea is that as a newer vampire they traveled to a larger capital city and was introduced to organized Kindred for the first time (in this case the Crones). She obtained her first dot in covenant status from meeting down there which then let her learn Cruac.<br /> We've talked and she thinks it would be cool if she brought Cruac back to this little town, and tried to get the other coterie member's to give it a shot. The part that I'm not sure about is the status dot in Circle of the Crone. I want to make sure that it comes up, and isn't just an additional cost to learning Cruac, all the while keeping it low scale. We talked about the potential of later taking dots in Mystery Cult Initiation, to have Ghouls and later mortals join a paganistic religion. Would her status in the Circle of the Crone only come up if they visited or is there a good way I could incorporate that?<br /> In the past I've allowed players to add their status dots into social rolls, but I fear that won't come up much this only a handful of Kindred in the town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than bring it in from another town, you could easily have the Crone reveal some aspect of herself to the vampire, during the embrace or while in torpor. She can learn Cruac without worrying about Status. I like the mystery cult idea. The vampire can cobble together a somewhat coherent system of belief based on her visions and shop it out to mortals eventually. There are a couple of mystery cults floating around in my city setting, where mortals led by ghouls believe the vampire cultists are lesser gods serving greater gods.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T05:35:21-07:00","id":927000,"title":"","content":"Something that came up when my group ran a CofD game set in a small town: While a smaller population means that vampires have to be extra careful with their feeding as any one of those 60k people turning up dead would garner A LOT of attention, it also means the vampires need fewer people in their collective pocket to effectively OWN the city. A mere 6-8 vampires could, with a handful of cleverly placed ghouls, applications of the blood-bond, and a smattering of Dominate, effectively neutralize any risk of Masquerade breech. <br /> <br /> Accidentally killed a vessel while feeding? Well, the local sheriff is your ghoul, and you've taught him the first dot of Dominate. He/she can mesmerize the coroner into falsifying the cause of death, pick up some drifter or junkie, and pin the murder on them. Those &quot;vampires secretly control everything&quot; scenarios that honestly feel a little to contrived as large-scale conspiracies (ala <i>Being Human</i> and <i>Blade</i>) work very well in a small town environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}